# GoldClub lab cabinet access (SMB + WinRM)

All GoldClub lab cabinets authenticate with the lab account **`GOLD-CLUB\test`**,
password **`test`** (lab-only credential — never reuse for production).

The interactive workstation user is **not** a local admin on every cabinet
(notably `10.0.0.171`), so without a stored credential, SMB and WinRM return
**"Access is denied" / System error 5**.

## Auto-apply (do this, don't ask the user to enter SMB creds)

SMB share access is made automatic by a **persistent `cmdkey` mapping** (stored in
Windows Credential Manager; survives logoff/reboot). If a `\\<ip>\c$\...` read or
WinRM call fails with access denied, register the cabinet first:

```powershell
cmdkey /add:<ip> /user:GOLD-CLUB\test /pass:test
```

Or register the whole known fleet at once (idempotent):

```powershell
.\Initialize-LabAccess.ps1 -Verify
```

Known cabinet IPs: `10.0.0.83`, `10.0.0.90`, `10.0.0.100`, `10.0.0.110`,
`10.0.0.112`, `10.0.0.171`. The working AFT reference cabinet is `10.0.0.90`
(`GST20664`); the credit-blocked target is `10.0.0.171` (`GST19737`).

## Remote execution (WinRM — do not use PsExec)

Use **WinRM** (`Invoke-Command`) for remote PowerShell on lab cabinets. It is much
faster than PsExec (~2–5 s vs ~40 s). Dot-source the shared helper:

```powershell
. "$PSScriptRoot\LabAccess.ps1"
Invoke-LabWinRmCommand -ComputerName $ip -ScriptBlock { hostname }
```

WinRM-by-IP requires the target in **TrustedHosts** on the workstation (added by
`Initialize-LabAccess.ps1` when run elevated). Port **5985** must be open on the
cabinet (`Enable-PSRemoting` / `cabinet_tools/usb_scripts/Enable-WinRM.ps1`).

Deploy to EGM: `.\deploy_egm.ps1` stages over SMB to `c$`, mirrors to `D:\` via
D$ SMB when available, otherwise via WinRM.

## Files

- `Initialize-LabAccess.ps1` — one-shot fleet credential bootstrap (cmdkey + TrustedHosts + verify).
- `LabAccess.ps1` — dot-sourceable helper: `Get-LabCredential`, `Invoke-LabWinRmCommand`,
  `Initialize-LabSmbCredential`, `Initialize-LabWinRmTrustedHosts`.
